  "recommendations": [
    "Add tight capacity tiers ahead of the existing profiles and keep the current profiles as fallbacks. This is additive and backward compatible: the tight proofs produce byte-identical public inputs and signatures.",
    "Keep CPS unchanged per tier so the public journal ABI, reader ABI pin, and statement identity do not change; only program/VK pins need adding.",
    "Run the existing per-profile constraint and boundary suites plus independent WASM verification before registering a tier, and pin its VK/program in worker.mjs, assurance-profile.mjs, prepare.py, package.py and native profile_fit.rs.",
    "If thermal testing accepts it, use 4 threads for the final proof (39% less wall time, about the same total CPU work). 8 threads is the knee for the largest tier; 16 adds 20% total CPU for 12% wall time.",
    "The remaining floor is witness generation (1.82 s for the largest tight tier) and protocol hashing (Poseidon2 + SHA-256 about 20% of gates). No micro-optimization found can remove the 250-character two-thread proof's remaining gap; chunked proving during writing is the architectural answer for that case."
  ],
